**Theorem 4.4 (literal D2 replay and structural extension).** The data in
PVC.6, together with the fixed public code/binding, identify exactly $h$,
including conversion, registry, own-code capture and all partial states.
The literal $\Pi_2$ lift has endpoint $\Gamma_2(Y(h))$ and transports each
lawful next native occurrence, with the same raw one-edge IN exits and
the same disabled nonexecutions.

Proof. Start RCA's word-encoded Step at the same primitive foundation.
Reconstruct only the canonical original packet from the extracted seed
and $H$. Feed the original fixed boot/preparation inputs, then $J_0$ at
old variable INs. If $A\ne\bot$, select the actual Install instrument
before ordinary row lookup at the old Ready with exactly $A$ completed
frames. Feed fixed $E(L)$, captured $\Delta(D_2)$ frame and the corresponding
serialized $E(D_2)$ at their distinct installation kinds. Before DONE
lookup remains in the active bootstrap, with partial new bits retained
separately. Afterwards feed $J_1$ only at installed variable INs. Stop
after the extracted $n$ rows.

Prove the assertion by induction on that native row count. The base is
the original primitive entrance. Equal pre-row raw records and the selected
input give equal RD, WR, adjacent moves, EX, BF, IN, OUT, TOK, CTL and
boot constructors by RCA Proposition 12.5's explicit local transformations.
Its receipt rule preserves the updated meter read head in the alias case.
The only extra instrument choice was fixed by $A$. All other choices of
$D_2$ are row tests on these same data.

In particular Step has no Convert, Call, graph-materialize or register-map
opcode. It interprets the compiled native row implementing that work.
A represented converter's validation or replay loop is just more represented
RD/WR/etc. There is no call to a semantic self-Call while proving this
induction. Each represented row costs finite word operations even when
the semantic handler containing that row is long. Registry assignment,
its partial bank/descriptor cuts, post-ACK work and final frame update
are ordinary rows in the captured $\Delta(D_2)$, and are included before
the annotated final Ready.

Own-code reconstruction has no circular literal. $L,D_0$ are fixed
descriptions; the main description is the actually captured public code.
The fixed public code parameter used by the inverse is the same description
supplied at the original installation. At a historical pre-capture cut
its bits are prescribed later installation parameters, not secretly present
old cells. Simulation still constructs them only when their actual WR occurs.

Each induction step has finite list lookup/replacement. The finite $n$
loop terminates on the actual image and never consumes a future variable
bit. Consequently equal extracted data yield the same entire prefix,
native/auxiliary creation identities and endpoint.

For the structural statement repeat CSA §§3–4's local proof for the actual
finite location union $q_2$. Ordinary rows retain the identical bounded
cell and receipt templates. Fresh-bit rows use the optional socket
constructor, with the actual latched bit and active-table guard; unchanged
bit writes are still assignments. $D_2$ introduces more rows and finite
locations, but no new local opcode or unbounded primitive field.
Its finite rule enumeration is therefore exhaustive. Induction gives
the endpoint and commuting step equations. Both physical IN bits use
their actual latch/receipt template, without a canonicality filter.
Failed guards have neither native row nor patch. This verifies the changed
code, finite sockets, input partition and stop annotations, rather than
applying a fixed-$D_1$ theorem to a different runtime. ∎

